{"`forEach(async ...)` inside the `try` block is not awaited, so calendar/video deletions can continue after the function proceeds, and exceptions inside the async callback will not be caught by this `try/catch`. Await the work so failures are handled and deletions complete before continuing.": 0.9746871590614319, "Using `forEach(async ...)` means delete operations are not awaited; the handler can proceed to send emails/return before calendar/video deletions finish, and any rejection becomes unhandled. Use `await Promise.all(...)` or a `for...of` loop so side effects complete and errors propagate predictably.": 0.9844195246696472, "`getVideoAdapters` now awaits each app module sequentially in a loop. When `withCredentials` contains multiple credentials, this serializes imports and can increase latency. Consider importing/building adapters in parallel with `Promise.all` and filtering nulls.": 0.5918483138084412}